A||||1||JAMIE||Corroded wing fasteners||||1||
Z||000000||JAMIE||08-16-2000||11:50 AM||||The main wing section is attached to the wing stands by 6 screws - 3 in each stand. The screws are fed thru holes in the stands and into small threaded "female" recepticles that are embedded in the main wing saction. My problem is that these recepticles are all corroded and broken - so - there is nothing for the screws to screw into,ie just empty holes in the bottom side of the main wing piece.<P>Anyone ever have same problem? Any suggestions on how to fix? What is your view on somehow gluing stands to wing? Glue type? Other way to attach?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phoenix||08-16-2000||12:17 PM||||I had the same problem on my wing just last  month when I painted it.  I had to us a drill and a Dremel moto-tool to drill and grind off the screw heads. Once I had the stands off I could remove the rest of the rusted inserts from the wing. I then put in new riv-nuts and it was as good as new.||||reg||1
